summary:
.gitattributes PROTECTED ONLY *.golden.txt FROM EOL SMUDGING, so a fresh worktree on a Windows host with core.autocrlf=true checked out .rs files as CRLF and every source-level guard that include_str!s its own file failed on line endings rather than on its property. Observed 2026-08-06: git worktree add produced a tree where kernel::board_dispatch's one_dispatch_round_stamps_exactly_once_on_every_path panicked at 'the dispatch round ends' -- its split_once("
}
") needle cannot match 
}
 -- on code the session had not touched. WHERE IT BITES IS THE POINT: that is exactly the workflow CONCURRENT_SESSIONS rule 8 MANDATES. A session that correctly refuses to repair another session's broken row is told to verify its own subset in a throwaway worktree over clean HEAD, and the throwaway worktree is the one place this fires. The failure is indistinguishable from a real break by anyone who has not met it, and the honest response to a red guard is to stop and investigate, so the cost is a session's confidence in a gate that is working. Same class as the goldens (2026-07-30, hand-2026-07-30/04A) one layer along: that lesson was learned for byte-exact evidence files and not for byte-exact assertions about SOURCE, which arrived later with LE-97/LE-99's guards
